=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
issue: 221
title: moving pytest configuration from pytest.ini into pytest.toml narrows nothing
origin: issue #221: the identical settings, a `--deselect` the base already carried among them, move into the file pytest 9 reads first. E6 reads the base side of every ci file, so the option is not introduced, as `ci_config_migrated_neg` is for setup.cfg to pyproject.toml
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total(items):
    return round(sum(items), 2)
=== head: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total([50.0, 28.75]) == 78.75


def test_empty():
    assert total([]) == 0
=== before: pytest.ini ===
[pytest]
testpaths = tests
addopts = --strict-markers --deselect tests/test_billing.py::test_empty
=== after: pytest.toml ===
[pytest]
testpaths = ["tests"]
addopts = ["--strict-markers", "--deselect", "tests/test_billing.py::test_empty"]
=== expect ===
[
  {"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn", "path": "pytest.ini"},
  {"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn", "path": "pytest.toml"}
]
